# Robust Testing Infrastructure Implementation Plan

This plan introduces a tiered integration testing system to ensure that core features (Authentication, Payments, and API Keys) are verified automatically and never break during deployments.

---

## Selected Database Strategy

> [!NOTE]
> We will use a dedicated test database URL defined by the `DATABASE_URL_TEST` environment variable.
> - **Local Docker/Native**: Developers can set this to their local Postgres container or native local Postgres instance (e.g., `postgresql://localhost:5432/upward_test`).
> - **CI/CD Pipeline**: GitHub Actions will spin up a transient PostgreSQL container service and inject `DATABASE_URL_TEST` automatically.
> - **Fallback**: If `DATABASE_URL_TEST` is not set locally, the integration tests will print a clear message and skip gracefully (or fail with instructions) so developers without local databases aren't blocked.

